<title>UK: Allders climbs after trading statement.</title>
<headline>Allders climbs after trading statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Allders Plc opened higher on Wenesday after the UK retailer said trading profits for the 15 weeks to January 11 were substantially ahead of last year.</p>
<p>By 0830 GMT Allders shares were 12-1/2p higher at 172-1/2.</p>
<p>&quot;The figures were pretty good and the shares have reacted accordingly,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>Allders said like-for-like sales were 11.6 percent up in the 15 weeks to January 11. Overall sales grew 37.4 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;These sales increases, combined with strong gross margins, are resulting in trading profits substantially ahead of last year,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
